  "number": 81,
  "state": "closed",
  "locked": false,
  "title": "fix(intention): preserve isolation scope in L7 recall and dedup",
  "user": {
    "login": "u7-u7",
    "id": 116776533,
    "node_id": "U_kgDOBvXeVQ",
    "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116776533?v=4",
    "gravatar_id": "",
    "url": "https://api.github.com/users/u7-u7",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/u7-u7",
    "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/u7-u7/followers",
    "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/u7-u7/following{/other_user}",
    "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/u7-u7/gists{/gist_id}",
    "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/u7-u7/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
    "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/u7-u7/subscriptions",
    "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/u7-u7/orgs",
    "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/u7-u7/repos",
    "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/u7-u7/events{/privacy}",
    "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/u7-u7/received_events",
    "type": "User",
    "user_view_type": "public",
    "site_admin": false
  },
  "body": "## Problem\n\nTwo related tenancy bugs in the L7 intention path:\n\n1. **Cross-user recall.** Session-scoped searches (`session_ids`, or a single `agent_id`) build only `isolation_keys`; `user_ids` / `agent_ids` are `None`. `recall_intentions()` had no `isolation_keys` parameter, so it called `vector_store.search()` without any tenancy filter. On a shared store that returns every user's intentions.\n\n2. **Cross-user hard delete.** `_partition_duplicates()` bucketed only by `(memory_at day, valid_until day)`. Two users with a similar intention on the same day were treated as duplicates, and the losing node was hard-deleted through `vector_store.delete()`.\n\n## Fix\n\n- Forward `isolation_key` / `isolation_keys` from `BaseReadPipeline` into `recall_intentions()` and on to `vector_store.search()`.\n- Add `user_id` and `agent_id` to the dedup bucket key.\n- Add regression tests for parameter forwarding, cross-user recall, and cross-user dedup.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `pytest tests/test_intention_dedup.py tests/test_intention_recall.py` → 37 passed\n- Full SDK suite with the faiss/qdrant extras → 1312 passed, 26 skipped",
